THOUGHT: My previous `sed` edit clearly corrupted the `find` method signature. I need to restore that and instead make a minimal, correct change in `put(K,V)`: call `find(key, true)` into a local, then use `Objects.requireNonNull` on that local before dereferencing. After fixing the file, I’ll re-run the build and check that the total NullAway error count drops from 32 to 31 and that no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/gson && \
# Restore the original find(...) signature line in case it was altered
sed -i '129,132s/^.*Node<K, V> find(K key, boolean create) {$/  @Nullable\n  Node<K, V> find(K key, boolean create) {/' gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/LinkedTreeMap.java && \
# Cleanly rewrite the put(K,V) body to add a non-null assertion on created
python - << 'PY'
from pathlib import Path

path = Path("gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/LinkedTreeMap.java")
text = path.read_text()

old = """  @Nullable
  @Override
  public V put(K key, V value) {
    if (key == null) {
      throw new NullPointerException("key == null");
    }
    Node<K, V> created = find(key, true);
    V result = created.value;
    created.value = value;
    return result;
  }
"""

new = """  @Nullable
  @Override
  public V put(K key, V value) {
    if (key == null) {
      throw new NullPointerException("key == null");
    }
    Node<K, V> created = find(key, true);
    java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(created);
    V result = created.value;
    created.value = value;
    return result;
  }
"""

if old not in text:
    raise SystemExit("Expected original put(K,V) method body not found; aborting to avoid corrupting file.")
path.write_text(text.replace(old, new))
PY
&& \
./gradlew :gson:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && \
grep -n "NullAway" new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 && \
grep -n " errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

